@host = http://localhost:5294

### 1. Normal search on the secure endpoint (200, returns alice)
GET {{host}}/api/users/SearchSecure?username=alice

### 2. Injection against the secure endpoint (200, empty list)
# The parameterized query treats the whole payload as a literal username,
# so the attack simply finds nobody.
GET {{host}}/api/users/SearchSecure?username=admin' OR '1'='1

### 3. Injection against the vulnerable endpoint: INCIDENT RESPONSE (403)
# Without the middleware this would return every user in the table.
GET {{host}}/api/users/SearchVulnerable?username=admin' OR '1'='1

### 4. Destructive command against the vulnerable endpoint (403)
GET {{host}}/api/users/SearchVulnerable?username=x'; DROP TABLE Users; --

### 5. Normal search on the vulnerable endpoint (200, returns bob)
# Shows that legitimate traffic still passes through the filter.
GET {{host}}/api/users/SearchVulnerable?username=bob
